**REJECT** against WO-RUST-V1-APP-SHELL-01. Current source has concrete rendering and responsiveness defects, and the recorded evidence does not identify the exact tested candidate. No edits, tests, or GUI actions were performed.

1. **P1 — Text bitmap format contradicts its buffer.** [text.rs:334](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.cache/WO-RUST-V1-APP-SHELL-01/worker/rust/crates/vexel-platform-apple/src/native_window/text.rs:334) passes `0x4002`: 32-bit big-endian, **premultiplied-first** ARGB. The surrounding code supplies and reads premultiplied-last RGBA. CoreGraphics therefore interprets the wrong channel as alpha and writes channels the copy-back code misinterprets. This is a code defect, independent of live visual verification. The text context also uses DeviceRGB while the final presenter declares sRGB.

2. **P1 — Semibold requests italic.** [text.rs:255](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.cache/WO-RUST-V1-APP-SHELL-01/worker/rust/crates/vexel-platform-apple/src/native_window/text.rs:255) incorrectly identifies bit zero as `kCTFontBoldTrait`. Bit zero is italic; bold is bit one. The implementation provides neither the requested semibold weight nor reliable weight fallback.

3. **P1 — Valid compact geometry can reject the entire frame.** `Layout::new(900, 300, …)` succeeds and includes the inspector. Its “Transform” label starts at `48 + 318 = 366`, outside the 300-point frame. The strict [text bounds check](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.cache/WO-RUST-V1-APP-SHELL-01/worker/rust/crates/vexel-platform-apple/src/native_window/text.rs:163) rejects it, and [render.rs:344](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.cache/WO-RUST-V1-APP-SHELL-01/worker/rust/crates/vexel-app/src/render.rs:344) rejects the whole redraw. The app then clears both dirty flags without presenting the new error status, leaving stale content or an initially blank window. Existing layout tests do not exercise this painting path.

4. **P1 — Text fallback and layout are incomplete.** [text.rs:272](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.cache/WO-RUST-V1-APP-SHELL-01/worker/rust/crates/vexel-platform-apple/src/native_window/text.rs:272) maps UTF-16 directly through one font and fails when any glyph is unavailable. There is no font cascade or shaped-line fallback; one unsupported tool symbol can reject the entire workbench. Advances are summed without shaping, wrapping, or ellipsis. The inspector’s multiword guidance is consequently a clipped single line despite receiving a 48-point-high rectangle. Baseline placement uses `size × 0.2`, without font metrics.

5. **P1 — Evidence is inconsistent and not bound to current source.** Individual logs record successful checks and tests, while `implementation-report.md`, `result.md`, and `cargo-output.txt` still report dependency-resolution failures. Two current hashes differ from the report:

