# WO-RUST-V1-APP-SHELL-01 implementation record

## Result

Addressed the five P1 findings from `sol-review.log` within the authorized app and Apple platform crates. This remains a launchable shell implementation; it does not claim V1 completion or visual acceptance. The root workspace manifest and lockfile match their source-seed hashes, and no dependency was added.

- CoreGraphics now uses the named `PremultipliedLast` alpha and `Order32Big` byte-order constants for the RGBA buffer. CoreText draws into a named sRGB color space, matching the presented frame's sRGB semantics.
- Semibold requests the named CoreText bold trait and falls back to the regular face if that face cannot be created.
- The inspector is omitted until its fixed rows fit (including at 900x300 and compact heights), and the painter also guards short panels. A rejected render writes a visible native window title and consumes the failed dirty state; a later event can retry rendering.
- Direct UTF-16 glyph indexing is removed. The private Apple text API creates CoreText attributed lines, uses CoreText shaping and system font fallback, wraps on word boundaries, places baselines using shaped-line metrics, and clips to the checked caller rectangle. Native handles remain private and no 5x7 scalar painter is used for shell labels.
- Added regressions for compact inspector geometry and RGBA copyback outside the clipped text box.

