I found a keyboard-path failure: the app never declares that it has no text-input target. A normal A/D key reaches `interpretKeyEvents`, whose text callbacks can emit `TextInputStateMissing`; the app treats that fault as fatal. The compact layout also still paints fixed-height rail, timeline, and inspector content beyond their allocated bounds.
